kg (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Shift-select by word and paragraph with Ctrl+Shift and the arrow keys
  * C-x 2 and C-x 3 split only the current window, like GNU Emacs;
    C-x 0 gives the closed window's space to its neighbors
  * Move between windows with Meta and the arrow keys (windmove)
  * Resize windows with Meta, Shift and the arrow keys; also C-x ^,
    C-x } and C-x {, and C-x + to balance the window sizes
  * Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn move to beginning/end of buffer
  * F1 opens help, F2 saves, F10 quits
  * Incremental search holds the view still for on-screen matches and
    recentres only when off-screen; motion keys and C-Space during a
    search hand off to the command, and C-r searches backward from point
  * Incremental search and query-replace fold case unless the query has an
    uppercase letter
  * Save keeps the previous version as a foo~ backup (M-x make-backup-files)
  * M-x require-final-newline adds a trailing newline on save (off by default)
  * M-x read-only-mode; read-only now also blocks mutating M-x commands
  * Fix UTF-8 text rendering as garbage in highlighted buffers

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:37:49 +0200

kg (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Visual mark mode: the region between point and mark is drawn
    in reverse video and tracks the cursor as it moves, with
    shift-select, CUA clipboard bindings (Shift+Insert/Delete,
    Ctrl+Insert), and rectangle mark mode (C-x SPC) with
    operations under C-x r
  * Emacs ido-style picker for M-x, file, and buffer operations.
  * Run external shell commands and pipe regions through them
    (M-! and M-|)
  * Detect external changes to open files; optional auto-revert
  * C-u universal-argument prefix, C-q quoted-insert
  * Tab completion in filename minibuffer prompts
  * More Emacs-style cursor motion (M-< / M-> / M-{ / M-} /
    M-m / M-a / M-e / M-r) and basename-only mode line
  * Bug fixes: Markdown highlighter crash on unmatched `**`,
    memory-safety issues surfaced by AddressSanitizer, paste
    auto-indent staircase

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 May 2026 17:36:19 +0200

kg (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Emacs-style key bindings for navigation, editing, search, and file
    operations; see 'man kg' for the full reference
  * Multiple buffers (C-x b, C-x C-b) with a shared kill ring
  * Split-window support (C-x 2 / C-x 3, cycle with C-x o)
  * Syntax highlighting for C/C++, Python, Shell, Ruby, Lua, JavaScript,
    TypeScript, React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, HTML, Markdown, and Makefile;
    language detected by file extension and `#!` shebang line; includes
    hexadecimal (0x), binary (0b), and octal (0o) integer literals
  * Multi-level undo (C-_)
  * Incremental search (C-s / C-r) and query-replace (M-%)
  * Paragraph reflow to 72 columns (M-q)
  * Auto-indent and bracket/quote autocompletion
  * Suspend to shell (C-z)
  * C-l recenters the view; repeated presses cycle top/center/bottom;
    also probes terminal size, useful on serial console connections
  * M-x command dispatcher with interactive Tab completion
  * Keyboard macros: record with C-x ( or F3, stop with C-x ) or F4,
    replay with C-x e or F4
  * Comment-dwim (M-;), join-line (M-^), word-case (M-u / M-l / M-c)
  * Exchange-point-and-mark (C-x C-x) and open-line (C-o)
  * Write-file (C-x C-w), insert-file (C-x i), revert-buffer (M-x revert-buffer)
  * Built-in key binding reference (C-h)

 -- Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Mar 2026 17:21:27 +0100
